---
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const page = await getEntry('pages', 'speaking');
const hero = page?.data ?? {
  eyebrow: '★ Fuel Woman of the Year 2025',
  heroHeadline: 'Speaking up for the ageing fitness community.',
  heroSubcopy:
    'I was named Fuel Woman of the Year 2025 for my advocacy work. Later that year I returned to the Fuel Summit to speak on how the industry should be coaching the 55-plus crew.',
  primaryCtaLabel: 'Watch the speech',
  primaryCtaHref: '#speech',
  secondaryCtaLabel: 'Read my piece',
  secondaryCtaHref: '#piece',
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Speaking — Coach Nikki, Fuel Woman of the Year 2025"
  description="Coach Nikki on stage at the Fuel Summit, talking about how the fitness industry should be coaching the over-55 crew. Plus press, podcasts and workshops."
  activeNav="speaking"
>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="speaking-hero">
    <div class="grid">
      <div>
        <span class="award-tag">{hero.eyebrow}</span>
        <h1>{hero.heroHeadline}</h1>
        <p>{hero.heroSubcopy}</p>
        <div style="margin-top: 28px;">
          <a class="btn-primary" style="background: var(--orange); color: #fff !important;" href={hero.primaryCtaHref}>
            {hero.primaryCtaLabel}
          </a>
          <a class="btn-secondary" style="color: var(--ink) !important; border-color: var(--ink);" href={hero.secondaryCtaHref}>
            {hero.secondaryCtaLabel}
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ph"><span class="ph-label">Photo: Nikki on stage at Fuel Summit, mid-speech</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE RECOGNITION -->
  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">The recognition</span>
      <h2 class="section">What "Fuel Woman of the Year" means</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Fuel is Australia's largest fitness business community for female coaches and studio owners.
        The annual Woman of the Year award recognises a coach whose work meaningfully shifts how
        their corner of the industry serves its clients.
      </p>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-top: 18px;">
        I won it for the work I've been doing to build strength training pathways for the 55-plus
        audience. The same audience the broader fitness industry largely overlooks.
      </p>
      <div class="speaking-grid">
        <div class="ph"><span class="ph-label">Award moment</span></div>
        <div class="ph"><span class="ph-label">Group shot at summit</span></div>
        <div class="ph"><span class="ph-label">Nikki with award</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE SPEECH -->
  <section id="speech" style="background: #fff;">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">The speech</span>
      <h2 class="section">"How we should be coaching the 55-plus crew"</h2>
      <p class="lead muted">Recorded at the Fuel Summit 2025. About 22 minutes.</p>
      <div class="video-block" style="margin-top: 32px;">
        <div class="play">▶</div>
        <span class="ph-label">Video player: Nikki's Fuel Summit speech</span>
      </div>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 16px; font-size: 14px; text-align: center;">
        Prefer to read? <a class="btn-secondary" href="#piece">Read the transcript →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SPEECH PULL QUOTE -->
  <section class="speech-pull">
    <blockquote>
      "We've spent decades telling people in their 60s and 70s to take it easy. The data, the
      bodies, and the lived experience all say the opposite. They need to be lifting, balancing,
      learning, and being challenged."
      <cite>From my Fuel Summit speech, 2025</cite>
    </blockquote>
  </section>

  <!-- THE PIECE -->
  <section id="piece">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Why this matters to me</span>
      <h2 class="section">A piece from me</h2>
      <div class="passion-block" style="margin-top: 36px;">
        <div class="ph"><span class="ph-label">Portrait of Nikki</span></div>
        <div>
          <p>
            My why started with my own ageing parents. Real talk: do they listen to much of what I
            have to say? Hmm, sometimes. But others surely have done, and they are thriving.
          </p>
          <p>
            Every body that walks into the studio tells a story through how it moves. I love
            watching that story unfold, finding the gaps, and building strength back into the joints
            and tissues that everyday life depends on.
          </p>
          <p>
            When I started this work, I noticed the industry had a blind spot. The 20-somethings get
            coached. The recovery-from-injury crowd get coached. The hardcore competition crowd get
            coached. But the 60-year-old who wants to keep lifting their grandkids, walking up
            hills, and travelling without their body letting them down? That person has been told to
            "take it easy", or simply hasn't been shown movement in a way that's been understood for
            them. Our bodies are adaptation machines. They'll adapt to the good and the not-so-good
            movement mechanics we throw at them. Everyone deserves the right to learn how to move
            well.
          </p>
          <p>
            That's the audience the Fuel Summit speech was about. And it's the audience the
            "Strong and Sassy: The Classics" sessions at the studio are built for.
          </p>
          <p>
            Ageing is a privilege, and not everyone gets the luxury of experiencing it. Strength
            isn't reserved for the youthful with loads of time. It's a foundation that protects
            independence, joy, and the ability to do the things that make your little heart dance,
            for as long as YOU want.
          </p>
          <p>
            If that resonates with you, or with someone you love, come and find me in Matraville.
          </p>
          <div style="margin-top: 32px;">
            <a class="btn-primary" href="/get-started">Book an intro session</a>
            <a class="btn-secondary" href="/sassy-seniors">See the Sassy Seniors programme</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PRESS / FURTHER READING -->
  <section style="background: #fff;">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Press · further reading</span>
      <h2 class="section">Elsewhere on the topic</h2>
      <div class="blog-list">
        <a class="post">
          <div class="ph"><span class="ph-label">Article thumbnail</span></div>
          <div class="date">Fuel Magazine · 2025</div>
          <h3>The case for strength training after 55</h3>
          <p>My contributed feature on why the industry needs to change how it speaks to ageing clients.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="post">
          <div class="ph"><span class="ph-label">Podcast thumbnail</span></div>
          <div class="date">Industry podcast · 2025</div>
          <h3>Building a studio that the 55-plus crew want to walk into</h3>
          <p>A conversation on programme design, intake, and the language I use with senior clients.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="post">
          <div class="ph"><span class="ph-label">Workshop thumbnail</span></div>
          <div class="date">Coach training · 2026</div>
          <h3>Workshop: coaching the senior client</h3>
          <p>One-day workshop for coaches and studio owners on running effective strength programmes for the 55+ audience.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FINAL CTA -->
  <section class="cta-strip">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Want to train with me?</h2>
      <p>
        The "Strong and Sassy: The Classics" sessions run four mornings a week at my Matraville
        studio. Start with a three-session intro and I'll take it from there.
      </p>
      <a class="btn-primary" href="/get-started">Book your intro</a>
      <a
        class="btn-secondary"
        style="color: #fff !important; border-color: #fff; margin-left: 8px;"
        href="/timetable"
      >
        See the timetable
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
